# Proxy Server Specific Requirements
#
# Inherits the ROOT direct-dependency set (../requirements.in), not the root
# lock. `-r ../requirements.txt` pinned the whole root lock as direct inputs,
# which dragged the torch/CUDA closure (torch, nvidia-*, cuda-toolkit, triton,
# transformers, sentence-transformers) into this CPU-only PII proxy image.
#
# Root pins are applied as constraints (`-c requirements.txt`, see the compile
# command in proxy/requirements.txt) so every shared package resolves to the
# same version as the root lock. The ML trio is removed from the graph by
# proxy/requirements-overrides.txt -- the proxy's PII path is Presidio + spaCy
# (shared/security/ner_filter.py) and needs no torch/transformers.
-r ../requirements.in

